Appendix G. Properties of the Projection onto $\Theta = [0, \theta_{\max}]^m$

For the reader’s convenience, we collect the elementary properties of the projection $\mathrm{proj}_\Theta$ defined on the box $\Theta = \prod_{i=1}^m [0, \theta_{\max}]$.

· Explicit formula: $(\mathrm{proj}_\Theta(\theta))_i = \min\{\max\{\theta_i, 0\}, \theta_{\max}\}$.
· Firm non‑expansiveness: $\|\mathrm{proj}_\Theta(\theta_1) - \mathrm{proj}_\Theta(\theta_2)\|^2 \le \langle \theta_1 - \theta_2, \mathrm{proj}_\Theta(\theta_1) - \mathrm{proj}_\Theta(\theta_2) \rangle$.
· Idempotence: $\mathrm{proj}_\Theta \circ \mathrm{proj}_\Theta = \mathrm{proj}_\Theta$.
· Projection onto a box is a truncation, which can be implemented with elementary min/max operations, making it suitable for real‑time embedded control.

These properties guarantee that the update rule (C.1) is well‑behaved and preserves the safety invariant.

